--- body ---
## Context

Per the user's request: "Idempotency: verify command tests cover it explicitly, add what's missing."

Already covered in existing test suites:
- `close` on already-closed ticket → `test_close.sh` (CLOSED already, exit 0)
- `tag` twice → `test_tag.sh` (TAGGED already, no duplicate header)
- `untag` on untagged → `test_tag.sh` (NOT TAGGED, no-op)
- `migrate` twice → `test_migrate.sh` (second run: no-op, already-clean count)
- `archive` no-clobber → `test_datasafety.sh` (destination exists: source preserved)

Gaps found:

**`erg rm` on already-deleted ticket** — what exit code and message? The test suite covers `rm`
on a ticket with dependents (DAG guard) and `rm --force`, but not `rm DELETED_ID` where the
file is already gone. Expected: non-zero exit, message on stderr, nothing written.

**`erg archive` second-run exit code** — `test_datasafety.sh` asserts source is preserved when
destination exists, but does not assert the exit code of the second `archive` run. The current
code logs a skip message to stderr and continues — exit 0 or exit 1? This should be pinned.

**`erg init` twice** — `test_init.sh` covers init on a fresh dir, but not init on an already-
initialized dir. Does `init` overwrite `.ergrc`, `AGENTS.md`, `spec-erg-v1.md`? Overwriting would
silently discard user edits. Expected: refuse to overwrite existing files (or skip with a message),
exit non-zero if any file would be clobbered.

## Implementation notes (plan phase)

- `installAssets` signature: add `refuseDiverged bool` parameter; add `skipped int` return
  value. `cmdInit` calls with `true`; `migrate.go:206` calls with `false` (update that call
  site: add `false`, use `_` to discard `skipped`). Exactly two callers confirmed.
- `cmdInit`: if `skipped > 0`, exit 1 after printing the count line
- `helpInit`: update text to remove "or refreshes" and describe refuse-on-diverged behavior
- Run `make docs` after changing `helpInit`: `test_docs.sh` gates on freshness
- `docs/erg-manual.md` is a regenerated artifact — if 0170 merges first, re-run `make docs`
  after rebasing (no true conflict, just stale artifact)

## Findings from imagine phase

- **`rm` on deleted file**: behavior already correct (non-zero exit, stderr message via resolver).
  Test gap only — the existing test uses a never-created ID, not a file-was-there-then-deleted ID.
- **`archive` second run**: already exits 0 on collision (skip-and-continue). Test gap only —
  existing collision tests suppress or ignore exit code; needs an explicit `rc` assertion.
- **`init` twice**: **behavior change required**. `installAssets` in `init.go` lines 55-68
  currently overwrites files that differ from the embedded asset (`refreshed++`). The ticket
  requires it to refuse/skip user-edited files. Trigger condition met: fix in this PR.
  Also: help text says "Writes (or refreshes)" — update `helpInit` constant to match new
  refuse-on-diverged behavior.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `test_rm.sh`: write a ticket, delete its file manually (`rm FILE`), run `erg rm NNNN DIR`
      → non-zero exit, empty stdout (`2>/dev/null`), "no ticket found" on stderr
- [ ] `test_archive.sh`: add explicit `rc` capture to the existing destination-exists collision
      test → assert `rc -eq 0`, assert skip message on stderr
- [ ] `init.go` `installAssets`: when an existing file differs from the embedded asset, skip it
      with a stderr message and set exit code to non-zero (do not overwrite)
- [ ] `helpInit` constant updated to reflect refuse-on-diverged behavior
- [ ] `test_init.sh`: add test — modify an init'd file, re-run `erg init` → non-zero exit,
      modified file unchanged (byte-for-byte `cmp`)
- [ ] Each new test has a negative control (first run or unmodified-file second run succeeds)
- [ ] `make check` passes
